ults. The paper says all 6 pairs reach the threshold and that the reverse-direction pairs show no significance, which aligns with the registry's consensus threshold interpretation, though the raw data shows a couple of those reverse pairs do hit significance at the per-method level. The Fleiss' kappa values are harder to verify since I don't have an independent source file for those calculations, but the numbers seem reasonable given the context.\n\nThe main issues are that the artifacts folder has a stale copy of the paper and those kappa values can't be traced back to a specific output, so I'm flagging this as a warning rather than a critical error. The Table 1 cleanup is more of a housekeeping note.",
